< Labels & Selectors >

#how to set labels?

apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: pod-2
  labels:
    app: swiggy
    env: dev
    client: tcs
spec:
  containers:
    - name: cont1
      image: nginx
      ports:
        - containerPort: 80

| kubectl get po --show-labels |

# we can also give labels to already exsting labels

| kubectl label pod pod-2 app=zomato env=dev client=flm |

| kubectl get po -l app=swiggy | gives only the pods with labels app=swiggy |

| kubectl get po -l client!=tcs | gives all other except the pods with tcs as clients |

| kubectl label pod pod-2 client- | unabels the pod | removes the client label |

#two types of selector and set based selector. The above are equality based selector.

#set based selectors are for multiple labels

| kubectl get po -l 'app in (swiggy,zomato)' | gives pods with app labels as swiggy and zomato |

#Finally do not forget to delete the cluster after practice

| kops get cluster | gives the clusters created |

| kops delete cluster --name clustername.k8s.local --yes | deletes the entire cluster |















